@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# MaCSad Lean export acceptance
+
+The host reports strict primitive facts without selecting a supported logic.
+Only this LOGOS gate owns the first profile's source and assumption admission.
+
+## To leanExportStatus (transport: Bool, source: Bool, complete: Bool, status: Text, kind: Text, axioms: Int, levels: Int) -> Text:
+    If transport is equal to false or source is equal to false:
+        Return "invalid".
+    If status is equal to "resource-limit":
+        Return "resource-limit".
+    If complete is equal to false or (status is equal to "exported") is equal to false or axioms is less than 0 or levels is less than 0:
+        Return "invalid".
+    If (kind is equal to "theorem") is equal to false or axioms is greater than 0 or levels is greater than 0:
+        Return "unsupported".
+    Return "eligible".
+
+## Test: Lean bridge admits a complete checked closed theorem export
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, true, true, "exported", "theorem", 0, 0) is equal to "eligible".
+
+## Test: Lean bridge rejects untrusted or incomplete transport facts
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(false, true, true, "exported", "theorem", 0, 0) is equal to "invalid".
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, false, true, "exported", "theorem", 0, 0) is equal to "invalid".
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, true, false, "exported", "theorem", 0, 0) is equal to "invalid".
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, true, true, "elaboration-error", "theorem", 0, 0) is equal to "invalid".
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, true, true, "resource-limit", "theorem", 0, 0) is equal to "resource-limit".
+
+## Test: Lean bridge does not silently drop assumptions or universe parameters
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, true, true, "exported", "axiom", 0, 0) is equal to "unsupported".
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, true, true, "exported", "theorem", 1, 0) is equal to "unsupported".
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, true, true, "exported", "theorem", 0, 1) is equal to "unsupported".
+    Expect that leanExportStatus(true, true, true, "exported", "theorem", -1, 0) is equal to "invalid".
+    For all booleans complete:
+        Expect that leanExportStatus(false, true, complete, "exported", "theorem", 0, 0) is equal to "invalid".
diff --git a/logos/lean-bridge/src/lean_wire.lg b/logos/lean-bridge/src/lean_wire.lg
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5d7656788e2d5329f72a0492a738d4a33715b26a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/logos/lean-bridge/src/lean_wire.lg
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+# MaCSad Lean bridge scalar wire and local correspondence
+
+## To leanWireDecimal (value: Text) -> Int:
+    If length of text_bytes(value) is greater than 7 or allDigits(value) is equal to false:
+        Return -1.
+    Let number be parseInt(value).
+    If numText(number) is equal to value:
+        Return number.
+    Return -1.
+
+## To leanWireRefs (value: Text) -> Seq of Int:
+    Let absent be a new Seq of Int.
+    If length of text_bytes(value) is greater than 1024:
+        Return absent.
+    Let fields be split(value, ",").
+    If length of fields is greater than 128:
+        Return absent.
+    Let result be a new Seq of Int.
+    Repeat for field in fields:
+        Let number be leanWireDecimal(field).
+        If number is less than 0:
+            Return absent.
+        Push number to result.
+    Return result.
+
+## To leanCoreCorrespondence (tags: Seq of Text) -> Text:
+    Let mutable result be "".
+    Let mutable position be 1.
+    Repeat for tag in tags:
+        Let mutable target be "".
+        If tag is equal to "sort":
+            Set target to "Sort".
+        If tag is equal to "bvar":
+            Set target to "Var".
+        If tag is equal to "forallE":
+            Set target to "Pi".
+        If tag is equal to "lam":
+            Set target to "Lambda".
+        If tag is equal to "app":
+            Set target to "App".
+        If target is equal to "":
+            Return "".
+        Set result to "{result}{position}|{tag}|{target}\n".
+        Set position to position + 1.
+    Return result.
+
+## Test: Lean wire retains only exact bounded decimal scalars
+    Expect that leanWireDecimal("0") is equal to 0.
+    Expect that leanWireDecimal("1000000") is equal to 1000000.
+    Let malformed be ["", "-1", "+1", "01", "1.0", "1e0", " 1", "10000000"].
+    Repeat for value in malformed:
+        Expect that leanWireDecimal(value) is equal to -1.
+
+## Test: Lean wire preserves reference order and rejects empty fields
+    Let values be leanWireRefs("0,1,2").
+    Expect that length of values is equal to 3.
+    Expect that item 1 of values is equal to 0.
+    Expect that item 3 of values is equal to 2.
+    Expect that length of leanWireRefs("0,,2") is equal to 0.
+    Expect that length of leanWireRefs("01,2") is equal to 0.
+    For all booleans valid:
+        Let mutable wire be "01".
+        If valid:
+            Set wire to "-1".
+        Expect that length of leanWireRefs(wire) is equal to 0.
+
+## Test: Lean wire constructor correspondence is explicit and ordered
+    Let expected be "1|sort|Sort\n2|bvar|Var\n3|forallE|Pi\n4|lam|Lambda\n5|app|App\n".
+    Expect that leanCoreCorrespondence(["sort", "bvar", "forallE", "lam", "app"]) is equal to expected.
+    Expect that leanCoreCorrespondence(["const"]) is equal to "".
